      '## The panel worth asking for',
      'Rather than TSH alone, a fuller picture usually includes **TSH, free T4, free T3, and TPO antibodies**, adding reverse T3 when symptoms are confusing. Pair these with the deficiency labs that drive thyroid symptoms \u2014 ferritin, vitamin D, and B12 \u2014 since low iron, low [vitamin D](go:thorne-vitamin-d-k2), or low [B12](go:pure-encapsulations-b12) mimic hypothyroidism. Our [T3/T4 guide](/hashimotos/t3-t4-guide-for-patients) explains the conversion pathway in more depth.',
